I can't open `.env.mcp` in this session. The only tools I have are the read-only bot-ops tools, and none of them read local files.

To see the keys, run this in PowerShell from the repo folder:

```powershell
Get-Content .env.mcp
```

To check which keys are set without printing the full secrets (handy if your screen is shared or recorded), this shows only the last 4 characters of each value:

```powershell
Get-Content .env.mcp | ForEach-Object {
  if ($_ -match '^\s*([^#=]+?)\s*=\s*(.*)$') {
    $v = $matches[2].Trim('"', "'")
    "{0} = ...{1} (length {2})" -f $matches[1], $v.Substring([Math]::Max(0, $v.Length - 4)), $v.Length
  } else { $_ }
}
```

To check that the keys actually work, I can run `list_bots` and `check_positions`. If they come back with exchange positions and stop orders instead of errors, the bot-ops server is loading valid keys.
